From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: appxdeploymentclient: answer PackageManager's package queries

Every PackageManager query returned E_NOTIMPL, which callers read as "this
system cannot say what is installed": winget's installed-packages source gave
up, and with it `winget list`, install and uninstall.

The FindPackages* family (for the user, by name and publisher, by family
name, with package types, by security ID) now returns a real
IIterable<Package> -- empty, because nothing deploys MSIX packages here yet,
and that is the true answer; FindPackageByPackageFullName finds none.
Deployment itself (AddPackageAsync and the rest) remains to be implemented
and will fill these results from the package repository.

